"""Replace only the obsolete POAM/RPCBF demo blocks; retain prior recordings."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,gzip,re,shutil,hashlib
import numpy as np
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2];OUT=ROOT/'output/full_learning_20261104'
SITE=ROOT.parent/'sites/belief-adaptive-monitoring/dist';DEST=SITE/'revised/data/full-learning-20261104'
DEST.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
def main():
    env_path=OUT/'cold/environment.json'
    if not env_path.exists():return
    env=json.loads(env_path.read_text());truth={}
    for s in (1,2):
        d=SITE/f'revised/data/scenario{s}';meta=json.loads((d/'metadata.json').read_text())
        nx,ny,_=meta['grid'];truth[s]=np.fromfile(d/meta['data_file'],dtype='<f4').reshape(ny*nx,3)[:,:2].tolist()
    cachefile=DEST/'render-cache.json'
    cache=json.loads(cachefile.read_text()) if cachefile.exists() else {}
    groups=[];summaries={}
    for kind,title,description in [
        ('pathawarebase-baseline1','New comparison · Baseline 1: global learning → 300 s MBD','Fresh run using task-cost forecast validation and safety-aware finalist selection. Learn wind over all free space until the previously calibrated whole-map RMSE threshold; validate three 15-second monitoring forecasts, then execute 300 s of MBD. Contact-free sampled forecasts may require RPCBF relaxation; relaxation and actual contacts are reported. The robot, wind, full POAM, clarity objective, actuator limits and execution filter are retained.'),
        ('pathawaremask-pathmask','New comparison · Proposed: candidate-path learning → MBD','Weight full-GP expected variance reduction along the original geometric routes by their destination monitoring need. This includes transit passages, not just Regions A and B. Use the calibrated 1.10 m/s task-weighted posterior vector uncertainty trigger, followed by the same task-cost forecast validation as the baseline. Use the same MBD and total mission time. These recordings test the proposed mechanism; incomplete or failed runs are not successful results.'),
        ('pathbase-baseline1','Earlier baseline · Strict finalist validation','Preserved earlier settings: a separate validation rule requires zero RPCBF relaxation. Scenario 1 completed 232 s of global learning and 300 s of MBD without contact. Scenario 2 is an interrupted diagnostic. These are references under the earlier selection rule, not the fresh safety-aware matched comparison.'),
        ('pathmask-pathmask','Proposed · Learn wind along clarity-valued geometric paths','Use the original geometric alternatives to monitoring areas. Each full route, including its transit passage, inherits the monitoring need at its destination. A compact 0.25 m tube defines the acquisition domain; full POAM covariance ranks actual measurements by expected reduction of uncertainty on that domain. After validated learning, use the original MBD for the same total time budget as the baseline. This is an acquisition proxy, not an exact value-of-information calculation.'),
        ('pathcalibration-pathmask','Calibration · Candidate-path wind learning with RPCBF','Bounded learning-only diagnostic for the new path mask. Select Task mask to see both the weighted corridors and the candidate paths. These recordings calibrate a later MBD handoff using forecast accuracy; the zero threshold intentionally disables switching in this diagnostic. They are not completed MBD comparisons.'),
        ('pathpilot-pathmask','Archived diagnostic · Recovery deadlock reproduced','The first path-mask pilot exposed a shared recovery defect: after wind displaced the robot outside its recorded path tube, every reconnection was rejected because its starting point was outside the tube. The robot then held indefinitely. These pre-fix recordings are retained; they do not establish a performance result.'),
        ('durationconfidence-baseline1','Archived diagnostic · Wider safety bounds and stalled survey','Seven-sigma confidence experiment, stopped after 420 seconds without reaching Region A. It repeatedly stalled while the recovery controller requested motion. This is a failed diagnostic, not a completed baseline. The original three-sigma setting is shared by the new comparison; contacts and infeasible commands remain explicit.'),
        ('durationresolved-baseline1','Failed diagnostic · Resolved POAM variance, three-sigma safety','The survey reached A and passed its finite handoff checks at 270 s. A later MBD route encountered a 6.54-sigma wind innovation and contacted the lower boundary at 291.165 s. The batch stopped. This is an archived incomplete experiment, not the requested finished comparison.'),
        ('durationsupport-baseline1','Diagnostic · Shorter kernel before inducing-support repair','Preserved survey diagnostic. The shorter kernel improved local prediction calibration, but the original first-pivot tie ordering could omit current measurements, leaving residual uncertainty despite repeated sampling. This record predates the inducing-support and direct-variance corrections.'),
        ('durationfailed-baseline1','Failed diagnostic · Original kernel at a sharp wind transition','Preserved diagnostic. The original full-posterior MBD passed its initial held-out handoff checks, but later entered an insufficiently learned sharp wind transition. The true wind left the three-sigma envelope and Scenario 1 contacted the lower boundary. The batch was stopped for diagnosis; no completed safe mission is claimed.'),
        ('durationbase-baseline1','Baseline 1 · Validate learned wind, then 300 s of MBD','Learn wind throughout free space from actual robot measurements with the shared POAM and RPCBF. The simulation-only handoff requires the validated whole-map RMSE threshold (S1: 1.25 m/s; S2: 2.01 m/s), plus held-out 15-second forecast checks from the current state and A/B. Continue the same state, clarity and belief for a full 300 seconds of original MBD. The whole-map thresholds are not claims of accurate wind everywhere.'),
        ('durationmask-routeprecision','Proposed · Clarity-masked learning, matched total time','Rank measurement waypoints by full-GP expected variance reduction weighted by predicted clarity deficit and geometric travel distance. Keep the declared finite-route posterior precision criterion of 0.20 m/s and the same additional held-out forecast checks, then use original MBD. Total simulated time matches Baseline 1 in each scenario. There is no additional 0.4 m/s² admissibility screen or adaptive relearning loop; RPCBF retains the full posterior uncertainty. Different handoff domains mean this comparison does not isolate acquisition weighting alone.'),
        ('cold','1 · Learn wind: uncertainty waypoints + RPCBF','No initial measurements. POAM is updated from the moving robot’s actual noisy measurements. The waypoint policy targets posterior uncertainty. It retreats along its measured path when the learned wind bound threatens control authority. Every command passes through RPCBF and obstacle/wall braking constraints. The baseline switches to MBD only if whole-map wind RMSE reaches 0.20 m/s.'),
        ('learned','2 · MBD with a measured wind map + RPCBF','A separate control experiment starts with the POAM learned from the full-coverage measurement test. It is not a flown initial survey. The 15-second MBD horizon, actual wind measurements and full posterior uncertainty remain active during the 300-second mission.'),
        ('mask','3 · Clarity-deficit mask → MBD','A new experiment starts without wind measurements and selects uncertainty waypoints weighted by the predicted clarity deficit. The no-sensing clarity prediction uses the existing dynamics over the 15-second horizon. It switches to the same MBD only when task-weighted vector posterior uncertainty is at most 0.20 m/s. True task error is displayed for diagnosis; it does not choose waypoints or trigger this handoff.'),
        ('correlated','4 · Correlation-aware task learning → MBD','The same clarity mask, with expected reduction of task-weighted posterior variance used to rank 32 candidate measurements. Full spatial POAM covariance includes the conditional residual. A measurement outside the mask can be valuable through spatial correlation. Every actual command uses the same safety filter. The acquisition is a bounded one-measurement design rule, not exact long-term monitoring value.'),
        ('routes','5 · Route-relevant wind learning → MBD','This acquisition also covers the existing geometric alternatives to areas needing sensing. Route occupancy is weighted by monitoring need and the expected squared sensitivity of wind acceleration to air velocity. Full POAM cross-covariance ranks 32 measurements. This tests whether accounting for transit passages improves on a clarity-only mask. The model, MBD and execution filter are unchanged.'),
        ('matched-baseline1','Matched comparison · Baseline 1: learn everywhere','Shared corrected recovery, identical sensor-noise sequences for each initial seed, full spatial POAM, physical dynamics and RPCBF. Readings are taken at each method’s actual robot position. Select high-uncertainty waypoints throughout free space. Begin MBD only if whole-map diagnostic RMSE reaches 0.20 m/s.'),
        ('matched-mask','Matched comparison · Clarity-deficit mask','Same common implementation as the matched baseline. Only the waypoint priority and handoff domain change: clarity deficit weights posterior wind variance. Begin MBD when task-weighted vector posterior uncertainty is at most 0.20 m/s. True task error is evaluated independently.'),
        ('matched-correlated','Matched comparison · Correlation-aware clarity mask','Use the expected reduction of task-weighted posterior variance from one noisy observation. Evaluate 32 spatially distinct candidate measurements, respecting the learned nominal reachability graph. Full POAM spatial covariance is retained. The handoff threshold is the same as the clarity-mask experiment.'),
        ('matched-routes','Matched comparison · Route-relevant uncertainty','Extend task relevance to the existing geometric routes, weighted by monitoring need and the expected squared wind-force sensitivity. Rank measurements by their correlation-aware reduction of uncertainty over those routes. This is a geometric performance proxy, not a proven value-of-information objective.'),
        ('information-baseline1','Filtered sensing paths · Learn wind everywhere','Score six geometric sensing paths plus hold by the expected reduction of whole-map posterior variance. Candidate paths stop before their current learned holding-force bound exceeds 75% of actuator authority. A five-second forecast applies the full dynamics and hard RPCBF under two training fields and a separate two-field validation bank. Replan each second from actual measurements. Begin the unchanged 15-second MBD only if whole-map RMSE reaches 0.20 m/s.'),
        ('information-mask','Filtered sensing paths · Learn where clarity is needed','The same filtered-path acquisition, weighted by predicted clarity deficit. The information score uses full POAM covariance at the actual predicted sensor positions, including repeated-reading effects. This is a finite-horizon design rule with a frozen kernel, not an exact monitoring value of information. Begin MBD only if task-weighted posterior uncertainty reaches 0.20 m/s; true task error remains an independent diagnostic.'),
        ('reachable-baseline1','Control-supported waypoints · Learn wind everywhere','Rank 32 candidate measurements by full-GP integrated variance reduction, accounting for geometric travel distance. Candidates lie in the currently connected part of a 0.05 m initialization graph with sufficient holding-force and braking margins under the learned confidence bounds. Actual dynamics, measurements, POAM and execution RPCBF are unchanged. This geometric screen is not a dynamic safety guarantee. Begin MBD at whole-map RMSE 0.20 m/s.'),
        ('reachable-mask','Control-supported waypoints · Clarity-deficit weighting','The same inexpensive active waypoint method, with variance reduction weighted by predicted clarity deficit. It can return through measured space to another sensing frontier. It does not optimize simulated trajectories during wind learning; every actual command still uses full RPCBF. The separate monitoring stage uses the original 15-second MBD after task-weighted posterior uncertainty reaches 0.20 m/s.'),
        ('global-baseline1','Global information goals · Baseline 1 · superseded diagnostic','Persistent distant goals with a currently supported local path prefix. This diagnostic predates the recovery-lookahead repair. Its actual recordings are retained; incomplete runs are not presented as full missions.'),
        ('global-mask','Global information goals · Clarity mask · superseded diagnostic','Clarity-deficit weighting of full-GP information gain. This 300-second diagnostic exposed a recovery-reference defect and did not start MBD. Corrected experiments follow below.'),
        ('adaptive-baseline1','Measured route bounds · Baseline 1','Learn wind everywhere using persistent global information goals. Route initialization avoids locally measured locations whose learned confidence bound exceeds the recovery actuator reserve. Full POAM, actual measurements and execution RPCBF are unchanged. MBD starts only at whole-map RMSE ≤ 0.20 m/s.'),
        ('adaptive-mask','Measured route bounds · Clarity-weighted learning','The same navigation and estimation implementation, with full-GP variance reduction weighted by the predicted clarity deficit. The separate MBD stage requires task-weighted vector posterior uncertainty ≤ 0.20 m/s. Recovery interpolation is corrected; temporary recovery still resets the information goal in this diagnostic.'),
        ('diversified-baseline1','Persistent route alternatives · Baseline 1','Global wind-learning objective. Keep the information goal through recovery; if measured geometric progress is below 0.30 m over 15 s, use existing geometry-derived bottleneck cuts to initialize an alternative passage to that goal. These temporary search cuts do not change obstacles, GP information or RPCBF. Whole-map RMSE must reach 0.20 m/s before MBD.'),
        ('diversified-mask','Persistent route alternatives · Clarity-weighted learning','Use the same corrected navigation, with expected GP variance reduction weighted by predicted clarity deficit. Alternative passages are tried after observed lack of progress. Full posterior uncertainty remains in execution RPCBF. Task-weighted vector posterior uncertainty must reach 0.20 m/s before the separate original MBD stage.'),
        ('precision-routeprecision','Route precision → original MBD · diagnostic','Same clarity-weighted information acquisition and corrected navigation. Handoff requires posterior vector RMS uncertainty ≤ 0.20 m/s over unique initialization-grid cells intersected by the executed route and the remaining geometric path to the selected information goal. This finite route criterion is a stopping proxy, not whole-map accuracy. Full POAM uncertainty remains in the original 15-second MBD and RPCBF. Route error is measured independently and is never used for this decision.'),
        ('supported-routeprecision','Clarity-weighted learning → MBD with wind uncertainty checks','The route-precision handoff is retained. Each later MBD request must also support its newly chosen trajectory: bound nonlinear wind acceleration error throughout the full predicted path, cap it at 0.4 m/s², and retain enough unused actuator authority to compensate that bound. Select two distinct finalists from the already-evaluated MBD archive and recheck at every 0.05 s hard-filter prediction. The 43 training evaluations, independent chains, full POAM covariance and monitoring objective remain unchanged. This extra admissibility condition depends on calibrated confidence bounds; it is not a safety proof.'),
        ('targeted-routeprecision','MBD with targeted wind learning · new experiment','Start with the same clarity-weighted sensing and route-precision handoff. Subsequently, compare already-evaluated MBD candidates on the same sampled wind fields. If a lower-cost, nominally controllable reference is blocked by wind uncertainty and the accepted prediction stays within one sensing radius, resume actual wind measurements along that reference. Full-GP variance reduction is weighted by clarity sensing value and aerodynamic sensitivity. This is a declared acquisition proxy, not an exact long-term value of information. Recheck MBD every five seconds. The physical model, POAM covariance, 43 MBD training evaluations and actual execution RPCBF remain unchanged.'),
        ('opportunity-routeprecision','Lower-cost monitoring opportunities → targeted wind learning','Refine the previous experiment: moving within one region no longer suppresses learning when MBD predicts a lower-cost route elsewhere. Information queries must lie on a nominal reference inside free workspace; requests that already violate mean-wind actuator limits are excluded. Keep the information goal and geometric progress history across temporary MBD execution. Rank actual measurements by full-GP variance reduction weighted by the blocked reference’s sensing value and wind-force sensitivity. This is a finite acquisition proxy. The existing posterior, plant, monitoring objective, independent MBD chains and execution filter remain unchanged. All validation branches are compiled during the explicitly timed startup call.'),
        ('reroutediag-routeprecision','Route-progress repair · intermediate diagnostic','This diagnostic isolates the route-progress repair before direct posterior variance replaced interpolated variance for waypoint completion. It is retained as evidence and is distinct from the final matched runs.'),
        ('reroutebase-baseline1','Previous 300 s recordings · Baseline 1 · survey only','Fresh runs with shared navigation corrections: changing to a longer geometric bypass restarts the progress window instead of falsely abandoning the goal; waypoint completion uses direct POAM variance already computed at the candidate. Learn wind throughout the environment; MBD requires whole-map RMSE ≤ 0.20 m/s. The double integrator, stationary wind, POAM, clarity dynamics and RPCBF are unchanged.'),
        ('clarityfinal-routeprecision','Previous 300 s recordings · Clarity-weighted relearning and MBD','Keep the same monitoring opportunity trigger and MBD budget. During relearning, rank actual measurements by full-GP reduction of uncertainty weighted by predicted clarity deficit over all free cells, rather than only along one selected reference. This tests the requested clarity mask throughout learning. The shared direct waypoint variance, corrected route progress, spatial POAM, physical models and RPCBF are unchanged.'),
        ('reroute-routeprecision','Final runs · Reference-weighted relearning and MBD','Fresh runs of the lower-cost-opportunity learning method with the same shared route-progress correction. A lower-cost MBD reference blocked by uncertainty can request actual measurements where full-GP variance reduction is relevant to its sensing value and wind-force sensitivity. The route precision gate, physical models, actual measurements and execution filter are retained. Compiled validation callables are reused without changing the evaluated trajectories.')]:
        runs=[];sms=[]
        folders={'pathbase':'baseline','pathmask':'proposed','pathcalibration':'calibration180','pathpilot':'pilot90','durationconfidence':'confidence-survey-stalled','durationresolved':'resolved-variance-failed','durationsupport':'shortscale-survey-diagnostic','durationfailed':'baseline-pilot-failed','durationbase':'baseline','durationmask':'proposed','matched':'matched','information':'information_frontier','reachable':'reachable','global':'global_goals','adaptive':'adaptive_routes','diversified':'diversified','precision':'route_precision','supported':'model_support','targeted':'adaptive_information','opportunity':'opportunity_information','reroutebase':'final_baseline','reroute':'final_targeted','reroutediag':'reroute_progress','clarityfinal':'final_clarity'}
        folders.update(pathawarebase='safety-aware-baseline',pathawaremask='safety-aware-proposed')
        prefix=kind.split('-',1)[0];mapped=prefix in folders;method=kind.split('-',1)[1] if mapped else kind
        targeted=method in ('mask','correlated','routes')
        folder=ROOT/'output/task_learning_20261105'/folders[prefix] if mapped else ROOT/'output/task_learning_20261105'/kind if targeted else OUT/('cold_checked' if kind=='cold' else kind)
        if prefix.startswith('duration'):folder=ROOT/'output/matched_duration_20261105'/folders[prefix]
        if prefix.startswith('path'):folder=ROOT/'output/path_mask_20261105'/folders[prefix]
        file_method=method if targeted or mapped else 'baseline1'
        if (targeted or mapped) and not list(folder.glob(f's*-center-{file_method}.json.gz')) and not prefix.startswith(('duration','path')):continue
        for s in (1,2):
            source=folder/f's{s}-center-{file_method}.json.gz'
            if kind=='pathbase-baseline1' and s==2:
                replacement=ROOT/'output/path_mask_20261105/baseline-s2-directed'/source.name
                if replacement.exists():source=replacement
            if prefix in ('pathawarebase','pathawaremask') and s==2:
                replacement=ROOT/'output/path_mask_20261105'/(folders[prefix]+'-s2')/source.name
                if replacement.exists():source=replacement
                recovered=ROOT/'output/path_mask_20261105'/(folders[prefix]+'-s2-recovered')
                if (recovered/'summary.json').exists() and (recovered/source.name).exists():source=recovered/source.name
            if not source.exists():continue
            name=f'{kind}-s{s}.json.gz';stat=source.stat()
            signature=[str(source),stat.st_mtime_ns,stat.st_size,1]
            entry=cache.get(name)
            if entry and entry['signature']==signature and (DEST/name).exists():
                sm=entry['summary'];runs.append(name);sms.append(sm);summaries[name]=sm;continue
            r=json.load(gzip.open(source));sm=r['summary']
            # The viewer already selects the last frame at an identical time.
            # Remove duplicate visualization frames without changing playback.
            for key in ('belief_frames','clarity_frames','task_frames'):
                r[key]=list({frame['t']:frame for frame in r.get(key,[])}.values())
            if r['handoff']:r['handoff']={k:v for k,v in r['handoff'].items() if k not in ('posterior_covariance','posterior_mean','inducing','clarity')}
            temporary=DEST/(name+'.tmp')
            with gzip.GzipFile(temporary,'wb',mtime=0,compresslevel=3) as f:f.write(json.dumps(r,separators=(',',':')).encode())
            temporary.replace(DEST/name)
            shutil.copyfile(source.with_name(source.name.replace('.json.gz','-protocol.json')),DEST/f'{kind}-s{s}-protocol.json')
            runs.append(name);sms.append(sm)
            summaries[name]=sm;cache[name]=dict(signature=signature,summary=sm)
        complete=len(sms)==2 and all(s['completed'] for s in sms)
        stopped=any(s['contact'] for s in sms)
        status='A run stopped at recorded physical contact; it is not a successful mission.' if stopped else 'Both 300-second recordings are complete.' if complete else 'Full-duration rerun in progress. Displayed recordings contain only the time actually simulated; reload to load the latest checkpoint.'
        if sms and kind=='cold':status+=' MBD handoff: '+', '.join('S'+str(i+1)+(': reached' if sm['gate_reached'] else ': RMSE threshold not yet reached') for i,sm in enumerate(sms))+'.'
        if sms and targeted:status+=' MBD handoff: '+', '.join('S'+str(i+1)+(': reached' if sm['gate_reached'] else ': task-uncertainty threshold not reached') for i,sm in enumerate(sms))+'.'
        if prefix.startswith(('duration','path')):
            status=('Waiting for the matched-duration recording; no result is claimed.' if not sms else '')+' · '.join(f'Scenario {i+1}: {sm["simulated_seconds"]:g} s recorded; survey {sm.get("survey_duration_s",sm["simulated_seconds"]):g} s; monitoring {sm.get("monitoring_duration_s",0):g} s'+('; complete' if sm['completed'] else '; in progress' if sm['stop_reason'] is None else '; '+sm['stop_reason']) for i,sm in enumerate(sms))
        status_file=folder/'experiment-status.json'
        if status_file.exists() and kind!='pathbase-baseline1':status=json.loads(status_file.read_text())['status']
        groups.append(dict(id='gpv-'+kind,title=title,description=description,runs=runs,result=status,pending=not complete,
            planning_budget_s=2 if prefix.startswith(('duration','path')) else 1,
            absent_run_label='Not run in this diagnostic · see result below' if status_file.exists() else 'Queued · no recording yet'))
    # Final method comparisons reuse the same source recordings, not new runs.
    for scenario in (1,2):
        ids=['gpv-diversified-baseline1','gpv-diversified-mask'];selected=[];labels=[];sms=[]
        for gid,label in zip(ids,['Baseline 1 · global wind learning','Clarity-weighted wind learning']):
            group=next((g for g in groups if g['id']==gid),None)
            if group is None:continue
            name=next((n for n in group['runs'] if n.endswith(f'-s{scenario}.json.gz')),None)
            if name:
                selected.append(name);labels.append(label)
                sms.append(summaries[name])
        if selected:
            complete=len(sms)==2 and all(sm['completed'] and sm['simulated_seconds']==300 for sm in sms)
            groups.append(dict(id=f'gpv-comparison-s{scenario}',title=f'Scenario {scenario} · Baseline 1 versus clarity-weighted learning',
                description='Matched physical model, POAM, sensor noise seed, navigation and RPCBF. The learning objective and handoff domain differ. Global and task-weighted precision are reported separately; a missing handoff means MBD has not run.',
                comparison=True,labels=labels,runs=selected,pending=not complete,
                result=('Both 300-second recordings are complete. ' if complete else 'Recorded checkpoints only; unfinished trials are identified below. ')+
                    ' · '.join(label+(': MBD handoff eligible' if sm['gate_reached'] else ': learning threshold not reached') for label,sm in zip(labels,sms))))
    for scenario,variant in ((s,v) for v in ['precision','supported','targeted','opportunity','reroute','clarityfinal'] for s in (1,2)):
        ids=['gpv-reroutebase-baseline1' if variant in ('reroute','clarityfinal') else 'gpv-diversified-baseline1',f'gpv-{variant}-routeprecision'];selected=[];labels=[];sms=[]
        method=('Clarity-weighted relearning + MBD' if variant=='clarityfinal' else 'Reference-weighted relearning + MBD' if variant=='reroute' else 'Clarity-weighted learning · '+('route handoff' if variant=='precision' else 'MBD with uncertainty checks' if variant=='supported' else 'MBD with targeted wind learning' if variant=='targeted' else 'MBD with lower-cost opportunity learning'))
        for gid,label in zip(ids,['Baseline 1 · learn everywhere',method]):
            group=next((g for g in groups if g['id']==gid),None)
            if group is None:continue
            name=next((n for n in group['runs'] if n.endswith(f'-s{scenario}.json.gz')),None)
            if name:
                selected.append(name);labels.append(label);sms.append(summaries[name])
        if len(selected)==2:
            status=' · '.join(label+(': contact at '+str(round(sm['contact']['time_s'],2))+' s' if sm['contact'] else ': complete 300 s' if sm['completed'] else ': recorded to '+str(sm['simulated_seconds'])+' s')+('; MBD handoff eligible at '+str(sm['gate_time_s'])+' s' if sm['gate_reached'] else '; learning threshold not reached') for label,sm in zip(labels,sms))
            groups.append(dict(id=f'gpv-{ "route" if variant=="precision" else variant }-comparison-s{scenario}',title=f'Scenario {scenario} · '+('Clarity-mask comparison · 300 s' if variant=='clarityfinal' else 'Reference-weighted comparison · 300 s' if variant=='reroute' else f'Baseline 1 versus {"route-precision handoff" if variant=="precision" else "MBD with uncertainty checks" if variant=="supported" else "MBD with targeted wind learning" if variant=="targeted" else "MBD with lower-cost opportunity learning"}'),
                description='Same physical model, estimator, sensor seed, navigation and execution safety filter. Global RMSE and finite-route posterior precision are different stopping criteria. Only the route-focused variant may begin MBD before learning the entire wind map. Check route RMSE, actual monitoring cost, visits and contacts; lower uncertainty alone does not establish better performance.',
                comparison=True,labels=labels,runs=selected,pending=not all(sm['completed'] or sm['contact'] for sm in sms),result=status))
    for scenario in (1,2):
        selected=[];sms=[]
        for kind in ('durationbase-baseline1','durationmask-routeprecision'):
            name=f'{kind}-s{scenario}.json.gz'
            if name in summaries:selected.append(name);sms.append(summaries[name])
        if len(selected)==2:
            matched=abs(sms[0]['simulated_seconds']-sms[1]['simulated_seconds'])<1e-8
            complete=all(sm['completed'] for sm in sms) and matched
            groups.append(dict(id=f'gpv-duration-comparison-s{scenario}',title=f'Scenario {scenario} · Equal elapsed time comparison',
                description='Baseline 1 and clarity-masked learning use the same physical system, initial state, actual-measurement noise seed, POAM model, original MBD and execution RPCBF. The proposed mission gets exactly the baseline survey duration plus 300 s. All monitoring cost, including the survey, counts.',
                runs=selected,labels=['Baseline 1 · global learning → MBD','Proposed · clarity-masked learning → MBD'],comparison=True,
                pending=not complete,planning_budget_s=2,
                result=('Complete matched recordings. ' if complete else 'Only actual completed simulation time is shown. ')+
                    ' · '.join(f'{label}: {sm["simulated_seconds"]:g} s, cost {sm["integrated_deficit"]:.3f}, '+('contact' if sm['contact'] else 'no contact recorded') for label,sm in zip(['Baseline','Proposed'],sms))))
    for scenario in (1,2):
        names=[f'pathawarebase-baseline1-s{scenario}.json.gz',f'pathawaremask-pathmask-s{scenario}.json.gz']
        if not all(name in summaries for name in names):continue
        sms=[summaries[name] for name in names]
        complete=all(sm['completed'] for sm in sms) and abs(sms[0]['simulated_seconds']-sms[1]['simulated_seconds'])<1e-8
        terminal=all(sm['completed'] or sm.get('contact') or sm.get('stop_reason') for sm in sms)
        groups.append(dict(id=f'gpv-pathaware-comparison-s{scenario}',title=f'Scenario {scenario} · Global versus candidate-path learning',
            description='Same physical environment, initial condition, noise seed, full POAM, MBD objective and safety-aware RPCBF. Baseline learns globally then gets 300 s MBD; proposed receives the same total elapsed time. Survey monitoring cost counts. Check recorded completion, failures and actual A/B visits.',
            comparison=True,labels=['Baseline 1 · Global learning → MBD','Proposed · Candidate-path learning → MBD'],runs=names,pending=not terminal,planning_budget_s=2,
            result=('Complete equal-duration pair. ' if complete else 'Finished experiments with a recorded failure; costs cover different durations. ' if terminal else 'Actual recorded checkpoints; full comparison not complete. ')+
                ' · '.join(f'{label}: {sm["simulated_seconds"]:g} s; learning {sm["survey_duration_s"]:g} s; cost {sm["integrated_deficit"]:.3f}; '+('contact' if sm['contact'] else 'no contact recorded') for label,sm in zip(['Baseline','Proposed'],sms))))
    new_ids=['gpv-durationbase-baseline1','gpv-durationmask-routeprecision','gpv-duration-comparison-s1','gpv-duration-comparison-s2']
    latest_complete=all(any(g['id']==gid and not g['pending'] for g in groups) for gid in new_ids)
    primary_ids=new_ids if latest_complete else ['gpv-reroutebase-baseline1','gpv-clarityfinal-routeprecision','gpv-clarityfinal-comparison-s1','gpv-clarityfinal-comparison-s2']

    primary_ids += ['gpv-pathbase-baseline1','gpv-pathcalibration-pathmask','gpv-pathawarebase-baseline1','gpv-pathawaremask-pathmask','gpv-pathaware-comparison-s1','gpv-pathaware-comparison-s2']
    current_ids=['gpv-pathawarebase-baseline1','gpv-pathawaremask-pathmask','gpv-pathaware-comparison-s1','gpv-pathaware-comparison-s2']
    primary_ids=current_ids+[gid for gid in primary_ids if gid not in current_ids]
    for group in groups:group['primary']=group['id'] in primary_ids
    groups.sort(key=lambda group:primary_ids.index(group['id']) if group['id'] in primary_ids else len(primary_ids))
