    evidence='''<p>The physical wind remains spatial and constant in time. The double integrator, quadratic wind-force mapping, actuator limits, clarity dynamics and original RPCBF remain. Explicit obstacle-braking inequalities now accompany the existing wall inequalities; both use the same learned uncertainty bound and nonlinear wind-force support. All measurements are acquired at the executed robot position, every 0.2 seconds.</p><p>Numerical reuse caches deterministic kernel matrices, not old posterior predictions. Means, full variances and coherent fields refresh after every measurement. The cache was checked against the prior implementation: maximum field/moment difference below 3 × 10⁻¹¹. Kernel fitting uses four independent minibatches every 50 actual readings, matching the validated GP training cadence.</p><p>The two fields within each bank are antithetic draws; the validation bank is independent of the training bank. This finite-sample evaluation is not an exact expectation or a global safety certificate.</p><p>Every mission has its own wall-time guard. Planning deadline misses are recorded without truncating the diagnostic recording. An infeasible MBD selection uses the existing filtered hold fallback and is retried at the next planning call. Missed deadlines, infeasible commands and contacts remain failures, not safety claims.</p>'''
