        evidence='<h3>New experiment protocol</h3><p>Baseline 1 learns globally, then receives 300 s of original MBD. The clarity-masked method runs for the baseline’s total duration. Both retain full spatial POAM, actual-position measurements, physical wind, double-integrator dynamics, clarity objective and RPCBF. The new shared POAM kernel uses spatial scales 0.1, 0.2, 0.5 and 1.0 m, selected through actual-reading calibration and a replay of the failed transition. Current observations come first when the inducing-point prior variances tie, so repeated local measurements can reduce uncertainty at the measured point. Safety predictions evaluate the full POAM marginal variance at each predicted position, including the conditional residual. Mean wind and coherent sampled fields retain their existing spatial representation. The original profiles and failed recordings remain archived. No truth enters trajectory selection or the controller.</p><p>The baseline RMSE thresholds were selected from recorded-survey forecast validation and are rechecked at the actual handoff. A separate simulation-only test requires position RMS error ≤ 0.25 m, maximum error ≤ 0.50 m, monitoring-cost error ≤ 10%, no contact and no infeasible commands in three held-out 15-second MBD forecasts. At least one must travel 0.50 m. This tests a finite set of operating conditions; it does not certify global model accuracy or future safety.</p><p>The masked variant retains its finite-route uncertainty gate and must also pass those forecast checks. Its stopping domain differs from the baseline. Both use the original full-posterior MBD without the experimental 0.4 m/s² admissibility screen. The full uncertainty and robust circle/wall constraints remain in RPCBF.</p><p>Both use seven independent MBD chains, 15 s horizon, 43 search evaluations, two antithetic training fields and a separate two-field validation bank. The tested larger 78-evaluation search did not consistently improve the checks, so the original compute budget is retained. Timing includes separate POAM update, wind-field construction, geometry, search and validation. The comparison target is 2 s; compilation and diagnostic validation are recorded separately.</p><details><summary>Historical experiment details</summary>'+evidence+'</details>'
