        evidence='<h3>Current path-focused learning experiment</h3><p>The baseline values wind information over all free cells. The proposed method uses the original clarity-guided geometric alternatives and places a compact 0.25 m acquisition tube around each entire route. Its endpoint monitoring need weights the whole route, so a low-deficit transit passage is still included. POAM cross-covariance determines expected uncertainty reduction from each real measurement. A remote measurement can be useful through correlation; unrelated uncertainty has zero mask weight. The geometric tube is an explicit acquisition proxy, not a change to the physical wind or robot model.</p><p>The shared recovery repair permits an obstacle-clear reconnection when wind displaces the robot outside its recorded path. Every actual command retains RPCBF. The current comparison uses the original three-sigma bound; the wider seven-sigma diagnostic stalled and is archived. Neither setting is a deterministic safety guarantee. The safety-field cache reuses only the unchanged prior draw, recomputing the full posterior correction after every real measurement.</p><p>Baseline survey handoff is checked using the validated diagnostic RMSE thresholds and held-out forecasts. The candidate-path stopping threshold is being calibrated on that different domain. The 180-second calibration records deliberately disable MBD handoff; they must not be read as final comparisons. The intended completed comparison gives the baseline 300 seconds of MBD after its survey and the proposed method the same total elapsed time. Survey cost counts.</p><details><summary>Earlier experiment details and validation</summary>'+evidence+'</details>'
